        Hold `v` across frames: it stays alive (a GC root) until `release`.
    fn Vm.value(this: &Vm, r: Ref): Value
        The kept value; nil for `none()` or a released `Ref`.
    fn Vm.get(this: &Vm, r: Ref): Table
        The kept value as a table (an empty view when it isn't one).
    fn Vm.release(this: &Vm, r: Ref)
        Let go of `r`. Releasing `none()` or a `Ref` twice does nothing.
    fn Vm.getNum(this: &Vm, r: Ref, k: string): f32
        Field `k` of the kept table as an `f32` (0 when missing or not a number).
    fn Vm.setNum(this: &Vm, r: Ref, k: string, x: f32)
        Set field `k` of the kept table to the float `x`.
    fn Vm.newTable(this: &Vm): Table
        A new empty table. It stays alive until the running native returns (outside a native:
        until the next top-level call ends); store it or `keep` it to hold it longer.
    fn Vm.newArray(this: &Vm, n: int): Array
        A new empty array with room for `n` values (`n` is only a hint). Protected like `newTable`.
    fn Vm.intern(this: &Vm, s: string): string
        `s` as a string that lives as long as the VM (so the host may keep it, e.g. as a name).
    fn Vm.openLibs(this: &Vm, libs: int)
        Bind the built-ins of the `LIB_*` bits in `libs`. Open them before loading scripts: a
        script's names are checked when it loads.
    fn Vm.seed(this: &Vm, n: int)
        Restart the `pick` / `rand` sequence: the same seed gives the same values (replays).
    fn Vm.nextRand(this: &Vm): u64
        The next 64 random bits (splitmix64; the VM's own state, apart from `j3.rand`).
    fn Vm.randUnit(this: &Vm): f64
        A random float in [0, 1).
    fn Vm.setLibGlobal(this: &Vm, name: string, v: Value)
        The global `name` = `v` unless the host set it already (how `math` is added).
    fn Vm.passOn(this: &Vm): Value
        Fail the running native with the error a `vm.call` it made just returned (message,
        position and trace stay the callback's). Returns nil to return.
    fn Vm.openArrayLib(this: &Vm)
    fn Vm.call1(this: &Vm, f: Value, x: Value, out: &Value): bool
        `f(x)`; false (error pending, `passOn` it) when it failed.
    fn Vm.openMathLib(this: &Vm)
    fn Vm.mathFn(this: &Vm, m: Value, name: string, f: fn(&Vm, Args): Value)
        `math.<name>` = native `f` (errors name it `math.<name>`).
    fn Vm.openTextLib(this: &Vm)
    fn Vm.loadString(this: &Vm, name: string, text: string): Result<Value, Error>
        Compile `text` as chunk `name` and run its top level. Ok holds its exports table.
    fn Vm.loadFile(this: &Vm, name: string, path: string): Result<Value, Error>
        `loadString` of the file at `path` (errors name the path). The only place j2 reads files.
    fn Vm.load(this: &Vm, name: string, file: string, text: string): Result<Value, Error>
    fn Vm.compileAndRun(this: &Vm, name: string, file: string, text: string): Result<Value, Error>
    fn Vm.useModule(this: &Vm, name: string, out: &Value): bool
        The exports table `use name;` binds, from `resolver`. False with the error text pending
        (`use cycle: a -> b -> a` when `name` is still loading).
    fn Vm.destroy(this: &Vm)
        Give back all script memory. The VM is unusable after this.
    fn Vm.errText(this: &Vm): &Buf
        Start a new error message; append to the returned buffer, then return false.
    fn Vm.fail(this: &Vm, msg: string): bool
        An error with message `msg`; always false.
    fn Vm.failAt(this: &Vm, fi: int, pc: int): bool
        Give the pending error the position of frame `fi`'s instruction before `pc`, and the trace
        from there down (once: an error from a nested call keeps its own). Always false.
    fn Vm.error(this: &Vm): Error
        The pending error as a value (its strings are views; see `Error`).
    fn Vm.charge(this: &Vm, n: int): bool
        Charge `n` units of native work (bytes read or built, values moved) to the step budget,
        256 per step, so `stepsPerCall` bounds what natives do too. False with `took too long`
        pending; a native then sets `raised` (`chargeNative`).
    fn Vm.chargeNative(this: &Vm, n: int): bool
        `charge` from inside a native: false with the native failed.
    fn Vm.tooLong(this: &Vm): bool
        Out of steps: `took too long (over N steps)`. Always false.
    fn Vm.memFull(this: &Vm): bool
        True (with `out of script memory` pending) when the heap is past `Limits.heapBytes`. Called
        right after an op that allocated stored its result (an op that allocated nothing never
        fails here, so code that doesn't allocate keeps running at the cap), so every live value is reachable: the
